ttitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Have Got", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\"> have got + infinitive</span> to talk about obligation (something you must do) or talk about an arrangement for the future that is already made.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I have got to call this number. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have got to book a tour of the apartment.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We have got to clean the apartment for the next tenant.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Comparatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you compare two things you use a <span class =\"strong\">comparative</span>.  You can use <span class=\"italic\">as \u2026 as</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We can show that two things are equal using <span class =\"italic\">as + adjective + as</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are no differences between the two compared things. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> This apartment is as nice as the other one.<br /> This red couch is as big as the black couch.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When we use this structure, the first thing mentioned is 'less' than the second thing. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> This place is not as cheap as the other apartment.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bedroom "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a room for sleeping in "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a one-bedroom condo."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear when talking about an apartment. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "living room "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the main room in a house where people relax "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The living room has a large television. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " to furnish "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to provide things in a room "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is the living room furnished?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "refrigerator "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large piece of kitchen equipment you use to  keep food cool "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The kitchen includes a refrigerator. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "washer and dryer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a washing machine and a clothes dryer "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I have to buy a washer and dryer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "square foot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a unit of area equal to one foot by one foot  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The condo is 1,500 square feet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rent "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the money you pay to use a place that belongs to someone else "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How much is the rent?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "steep"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "high; expensive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's a little steep for me.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lease"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an agreement that allows you to use a building for a period of time, in return for rent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do I have to sign a lease?   "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tenant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who lives in an apartment and pays rent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have got to clean the apartment for the next tenant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le03ob09aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose two objects in your classroom.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare them. What is the same about both of them? What is different about them?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short paragraph (6-7 sentences) about them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">as ... as</span> and <span class=\"italic\">not as ... as</span> in your paragraph. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your paragraph. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your paragraph to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to their paragraph. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about objects in a room.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare things using <span class=\"italic\">as ... as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">not as ... as</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my paragraph aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to my partner's paragraph.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}